---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SectionHeader from '../components/SectionHeader.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Omnipeak — Custom software for small businesses"
  description="Omnipeak builds custom software for small businesses — booking and membership systems, internal tools, automations, and admin dashboards — and finishes projects other developers left half-done."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="hero__inner">
        <div class="hero__content">
          <span class="eyebrow">Custom software · Automation · Internal tools</span>
          <h1>Custom software for small businesses that outgrew their tools.</h1>
          <p class="lede">
            Omnipeak builds the software your business actually needs — booking and membership
            systems, internal tools, automations, the report you rebuild by hand every month.
            You'll work directly with the engineer building it, and you'll own every piece of
            it.
          </p>
          <div class="btn-row">
            <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn--primary">Book an intro call</a>
            <a href="/work/" class="btn btn--ghost">See the work</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hero__visual" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="sheet">
            <div class="sheet__head">
              <span></span>
              <span>Bay 1</span>
              <span>Bay 2</span>
              <span>Bay 3</span>
            </div>
            <div class="sheet__row">
              <span class="sheet__time">9:00</span>
              <span class="sheet__slot sheet__slot--booked">Booked</span>
              <span class="sheet__slot"></span>
              <span class="sheet__slot sheet__slot--member">Member</span>
            </div>
            <div class="sheet__row">
              <span class="sheet__time">10:00</span>
              <span class="sheet__slot"></span>
              <span class="sheet__slot sheet__slot--booked">Booked</span>
              <span class="sheet__slot sheet__slot--member">Member</span>
            </div>
            <div class="sheet__row">
              <span class="sheet__time">11:00</span>
              <span class="sheet__slot sheet__slot--member">Member</span>
              <span class="sheet__slot sheet__slot--booked">Booked</span>
              <span class="sheet__slot"></span>
            </div>
            <div class="sheet__row">
              <span class="sheet__time">12:00</span>
              <span class="sheet__slot sheet__slot--booked">League</span>
              <span class="sheet__slot"></span>
              <span class="sheet__slot sheet__slot--booked">Booked</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--dim">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionHeader
        eyebrow="Who this is for"
        title="Small businesses past what off-the-shelf software can do"
        subtitle="Owners and operations leads who have hit the wall — the tool almost fits but not quite, the workaround has become the process, or a developer left a half-built system behind."
      />
      <ul class="clients">
        <li>Outgrew spreadsheets</li>
        <li>Off-the-shelf almost fits</li>
        <li>Repetitive work done by hand</li>
        <li>Inherited a half-built system</li>
        <li>Data in five places</li>
        <li>Reports rebuilt every month</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--rule">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionHeader
        eyebrow="The ground rules"
        title="How you're protected"
        subtitle="Most clients come to Omnipeak after a bad experience with a developer. These four rules apply to every project, in writing."
      />
      <div class="grid grid--2">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>You own everything</h3>
          <p>
            The code, the repository, the hosting, and the payment accounts are in your name
            from day one. Nothing is held hostage if you ever part ways.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>You can run it</h3>
          <p>
            Every system ships with an admin screen built for a non-technical owner — change
            prices, manage records, and see what's happening without calling a developer.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Documented handover</h3>
          <p>
            Written documentation comes with the system, so any competent developer could pick
            it up tomorrow. You are never dependent on one person's memory.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>No lock-in</h3>
          <p>
            No proprietary platform and no monthly fee just to keep your own software running.
            Ongoing maintenance is available for as long as you want it — and optional.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--rule">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionHeader
        eyebrow="Recent work"
        title="The third attempt that shipped"
        subtitle="A multi-location golf simulator business hired Omnipeak after two previous developers failed to finish their booking platform. The rebuild handles reservations with time-based pricing, memberships with recurring billing, and is structured for franchise growth."
      />
      <p style="max-width: 44em; margin-bottom: var(--space-lg); color: var(--ink-soft);">
        Booking and billing is the hardest kind of small-business software, and where Omnipeak
        goes deepest — but the work ranges from internal dashboards to automations that replace
        a weekly manual routine.
      </p>
      <a href="/work/" class="btn btn--ghost">Read the case study</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTA />
</BaseLayout>
